.TH FATHOM_REVIEW 1  "fathom 0.1.0-alpha.1" 
.SH NAME
fathom\-review \- The review ledger: sign\-offs that outlive the history they were written about (`e4.6`)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfathom review\fR [\fB\-\-root\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The review ledger: sign\-offs that outlive the history they were written about (`e4.6`)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-root\fR \fI<ROOT>\fR [default: .]
The repository to read
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print the verdict and every entry as one JSON line (machine contract `fathom.cli.review/1`).

Global so `fathom review \-\-json sign …` and `fathom review sign … \-\-json` are the same command; a reviewer should not have to remember which side of the subverb a flag lives on.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
fathom\-review\-status(1)
The verdict: is every episode covered by a sign\-off that still matches (exit `7` when it is not)
.TP
fathom\-review\-sign(1)
Sign an episode off, appending one entry to `.fathom/reviews/ledger.md`
.TP
fathom\-review\-sync(1)
Render the queue\*(Aqs acts that the ledger has never seen
.TP
fathom\-review\-list(1)
List the ledger\*(Aqs entries with their verdicts
.TP
fathom\-review\-verify(1)
Re\-hash every entry against its own `digest:` line — tampering, and nothing else
